<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Gold Fields Namibia Q4 profit falls.</title>
<headline>Gold Fields Namibia Q4 profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-Dec 31 versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Net profit before capital</p>
<p>    spending			  24.41 vs  25.17 loss</p>
<p>    Capital spending		 6.24 vs   5.75</p>
<p>    Tonnes milled		  38,000 vs 278,000</p>
<p>Metal in concentrates produced</p>
<p>    - Copper (t)			768 vs 3,084</p>
<p>    - Lead (t)			  114 vs 1,068</p>
<p>    - Silver (t)			  9 vs     7</p>
<p>Metal produced from smelters</p>
<p>    - Copper in blister (t)	1,35 vs 4,53</p>
<p>    - Refined lead(t)		0,86 vs 3,94</p>
<p>Full name: Gold Fields Namibia Ltd (financial - mining houses)</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
